-- ===========================================================================
§§ `Order 2, Rules 8 and 9 -- affidavits of evidence-in-chief; applications in pending proceedings`
-- ===========================================================================

-- The Court's power is fixed to a window in the text's own words: after pleadings are filed and served, but before any exchange of documents
-- and before the Court considers the need for any application.  Outside the window the answer is JUST FALSE (ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)).
-- src:172 | 8. The Court may order the parties to file and exchange affidavits of evidence‑in‑chief of all or some witnesses after pleadings have been filed and
-- src:172 | served but before any exchange of documents and before the Court considers the need for any application.
@ref O 2 r 8 (src:172)
GIVEN `pleadings have been filed and served` IS A BOOLEAN
      `documents have begun to be exchanged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has considered the need for any application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 2 r 8 the Court may order the parties to file and exchange affidavits of evidence-in-chief` MEANS
    IF `pleadings have been filed and served` AND (NOT `documents have begun to be exchanged`) AND (NOT `the Court has considered the need for any application`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after pleadings have been filed and served but before any exchange of documents and before the Court considers the need for any application"

DECLARE `o 2 r 9(1) the matter` IS ONE OF
    `o 2 r 9(1)(a) addition or removal of parties`
    `o 2 r 9(1)(b) consolidation of actions`
    `o 2 r 9(1)(c) division of issues at trial to be heard separately`
    `o 2 r 9(1)(d) security for costs`
    `o 2 r 9(1)(e) further and better particulars of pleadings`
    `o 2 r 9(1)(f) amendment of pleadings`
    `o 2 r 9(1)(g) filing of further pleadings`
    `o 2 r 9(1)(h) striking out of part of an action or of the defence`
    `o 2 r 9(1)(i) judgment on admission of facts`
    `o 2 r 9(1)(j) determination of questions of law or construction of documents`
    `o 2 r 9(1)(k) production of documents`
    `o 2 r 9(1)(l) interim relief`
    `o 2 r 9(1)(m) expert evidence and assessors`
    `o 2 r 9(1)(n) independent witness and interested non-parties`
    `o 2 r 9(1)(o) independent counsel`
    `o 2 r 9(1) some other matter`

