DECLARE `o 2 r 9(8) the application` IS ONE OF
    `o 2 r 9(8)(a) an injunction or a search order, with any incidental matter`
    `o 2 r 9(8)(b) substituted service`
    `o 2 r 9(8)(c) service out of Singapore`
    `o 2 r 9(8)(d) setting aside service of an originating process`
    `o 2 r 9(8)(e) judgment in default of a notice of intention to contest or not contest an originating claim`
    `o 2 r 9(8)(f) judgment in default of defence`
    `o 2 r 9(8)(g) summary judgment`
    `o 2 r 9(8)(h) striking out the whole of an action or defence`
    `o 2 r 9(8)(i) stay of the whole action`
    `o 2 r 9(8)(j) stay of enforcement of a judgment or order`
    `o 2 r 9(8)(k) an enforcement order`
    `o 2 r 9(8)(l) permission to appeal`
    `o 2 r 9(8)(m) transfer of proceedings under the State Courts Act`
    `o 2 r 9(8)(n) setting aside third party proceedings`
    `o 2 r 9(8)(o) permission to make an application for a committal order`
    `o 2 r 9(8) some other application`

-- src:210-239 | (8) No other application may be taken out by any party at any time except as directed at the case conference or with the Court’s approval, unless it
-- src:210-239 | is an application for — ( a ) an injunction or a search order which may include an application for any other matter if it is incidental to the
-- src:210-239 | injunction or search order; ( b ) substituted service; ( c ) service out of Singapore; ( d ) setting aside service of an originating process; ( e )
-- src:210-239 | judgment in default of a notice of intention to contest or not contest an originating claim; ( f ) judgment in default of defence; ( g ) summary
-- src:210-239 | judgment; ( h ) striking out the whole of an action or defence; ( i ) stay of the whole action; ( j ) stay of enforcement of a judgment or order; ( k
-- src:210-239 | ) an enforcement order; ( l ) permission to appeal; ( m ) transfer of proceedings under the State Courts Act; ( n ) setting aside third party
-- src:210-239 | proceedings; or ( o ) permission to make an application for a committal order.
@ref O 2 r 9(8) (src:210-239)
GIVEN application IS A `o 2 r 9(8) the application`
      `it is directed at the case conference` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court approves` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 2 r 9(8) the application may be taken out` MEANS
    CONSIDER application
    WHEN `o 2 r 9(8) some other application` THEN
        IF `it is directed at the case conference` OR `the Court approves`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "except as directed at the case conference or with the Court’s approval" lifts the negative and does not grant a permission
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No other application may be taken out by any party at any time"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "unless it is an application for" one of the fifteen listed lifts the negative and does not grant a permission

