            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the requirement is for approval "to file further applications other than those directed at a case conference"
        IF `it is sought by letter` AND `the letter sets out the essence of the intended application` AND `the letter sets out the reasons why it is necessary at that stage of the proceedings`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has to be sought by letter setting out the essence of the intended application and the reasons why it is necessary at that stage of the proceedings"

-- Paragraph (10): the window is "starting 14 days before the commencement of the trial and ending when the Court has made its decision".
-- src:241 | (10) Except in a special case and with the trial Judge’s approval, no application may be taken out during the period starting 14 days before the
-- src:241 | commencement of the trial and ending when the Court has made its decision.
@ref O 2 r 9(10) (src:241)
`o 2 r 9(10) the period before the trial` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `Before the anchor`

-- src:241 | (10) Except in a special case and with the trial Judge’s approval, no application may be taken out during the period starting 14 days before the
-- src:241 | commencement of the trial and ending when the Court has made its decision.
@ref O 2 r 9(10) (src:241)
GIVEN `the day the application is taken out` IS A DATE
      `the day the trial commences` IS A DATE
      `the day the Court makes its decision` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `it is a special case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trial Judge approves` IS A BOOLEAN
      calendar IS A `Court calendar`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 2 r 9(10) an application may be taken out on that day` MEANS
    IF `the day the application is taken out` AT LEAST `o 3 r 3(4) the first day of a window within a period before a date` `o 2 r 9(10) the period before the trial` `the day the trial commences` calendar
       AND (CONSIDER `the day the Court makes its decision`
            WHEN JUST decided THEN `the day the application is taken out` AT MOST decided
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE)
    THEN
        IF `it is a special case` AND `the trial Judge approves`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Except in a special case and with the trial Judge’s approval" lifts the negative and does not grant a permission
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no application may be taken out during the period starting 14 days before the commencement of the trial and ending when the Court has made its decision"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the flat negative reaches "the period starting 14 days before the commencement of the trial and ending when the Court has made its decision" only

-- The period itself, as a yes/no (ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)): the text fixes it in its own words, "starting 14 days before the commencement of the trial and
-- ending when the Court has made its decision", so a day outside it is JUST FALSE.  The function above says whether an application MAY be taken out;
-- outside the period it answers NOTHING (the flat negative says nothing of other days), and this one says whether the day is inside the period.
-- src:241 | (10) Except in a special case and with the trial Judge’s approval, no application may be taken out during the period starting 14 days before the
-- src:241 | commencement of the trial and ending when the Court has made its decision.
@ref O 2 r 9(10) (src:241)
GIVEN `the day the application is taken out` IS A DATE
      `the day the trial commences` IS A DATE
      `the day the Court makes its decision` IS A MAYBE DATE
      calendar IS A `Court calendar`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 2 r 9(10) the day falls in the period in which no application may be taken out` MEANS
    IF `the day the application is taken out` AT LEAST `o 3 r 3(4) the first day of a window within a period before a date` `o 2 r 9(10) the period before the trial` `the day the trial commences` calendar
       AND (CONSIDER `the day the Court makes its decision`
            WHEN JUST decided THEN `the day the application is taken out` AT MOST decided
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the period starting 14 days before the commencement of the trial and ending when the Court has made its decision" (a period fixed in the text's own words)

