-- The number of sets of respondents for which security is to be given.  The text allows security "for the costs of the appeal of each respondent
-- (or for the costs of the appeal of each set of the respondents where the respondents are represented by the same firm of solicitors)"; it does not say
-- who chooses.  This function counts the SETS: respondents represented by the same firm are one set, and a respondent with no firm is a set of one.
-- The count of respondents taken one by one is just the length of the list.  Whether security is required at all (the "Save for" appeals of
-- Divisions 2 and 4 of Order 18) is the yes/no function `o 2 r 10(7) the appellant has to provide security for the costs of the appeal`, not this count.
-- src:250 | (7) Save for appeals filed under Divisions 2 and 4 of Order 18, the appellant has to provide security for the costs of the appeal of each respondent
-- src:250 | (or for the costs of the appeal of each set of the respondents where the respondents are represented by the same firm of solicitors).
@ref O 2 r 10(7) (src:250)
GIVEN `the firm of solicitors representing each respondent, with NOTHING for a respondent who has no firm` IS A LIST OF MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A NUMBER
`o 2 r 10(7) the number of sets of respondents for which security is to be provided` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the firm of solicitors representing each respondent, with NOTHING for a respondent who has no firm`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN firm FOLLOWED BY others THEN
        CONSIDER firm
        WHEN NOTHING THEN 1 PLUS `o 2 r 10(7) the number of sets of respondents for which security is to be provided` others
        WHEN JUST name THEN
            IF elem (JUST name) others
            THEN `o 2 r 10(7) the number of sets of respondents for which security is to be provided` others
            ELSE 1 PLUS `o 2 r 10(7) the number of sets of respondents for which security is to be provided` others

