        IF `the appellate Court approves`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "without the approval of the appellate Court" lifts the negative and does not grant a permission
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No document other than the parties’ written submissions ... may be filed in the appeal without the approval of the appellate Court"

