§§ `Order 2, Rules 13 and 14 -- costs; enforcement`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:269 | 13. —(1) Costs are in the discretion of the Court and the Court has the power to determine all issues relating to the costs of or incidental to all
-- src:269 | proceedings at any stage of the proceedings or after the conclusion of the proceedings.
@ref O 2 r 13(1) (src:269)
GIVEN `the issue relates to the costs of or incidental to proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 2 r 13(1) the Court has the power to determine the issue relating to costs` MEANS
    IF `the issue relates to the costs of or incidental to proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "all issues relating to the costs of or incidental to all proceedings"

-- src:269 | (2) The Court which heard a matter must fix the costs of the matter, unless the Court thinks fit to direct an assessment of the costs.
@ref O 2 r 13(2) (src:269)
GIVEN `the Court heard the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court thinks fit to direct an assessment of the costs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 2 r 13(2) the Court which heard the matter must fix the costs of the matter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Court heard the matter`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of "The Court which heard a matter"
        IF `the Court thinks fit to direct an assessment of the costs`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the Court thinks fit to direct an assessment of the costs"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

